Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:44:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH v2 2/2] phy: qcom: mipi-csi2: add SM8750 2.4.0 lane
 settings

The 3nm two-phase CSI2 PHY found on SM8750 ships the v2.4.0 lane table,
while kaanapali-csi2-phy currently reuses lane_regs_x1e80100[], i.e. the
4nm v2.1.2 values. Both tables have the same 103 register addresses and
the 13 differing data bytes fall into three groups:

  0x0000/0x0400/0x0800/0x0c00        0x8e -> 0x8c  (DEFAULT)
  0x0008/0x0408/0x0808/0x0c08/0x0e08 0x10 -> 0x19  (SETTLE_CNT_LOWER_BYTE)
  0x0060/0x0460/0x0860/0x0c60        0xbd -> 0xfd  (SKEW_CAL)

Only the four DEFAULT writes reach the hardware from this table:
phy_qcom_mipi_csi2_gen2_config_lanes() overwrites SETTLE_CNT_LOWER_BYTE
with the runtime settle_cnt and skips CSIPHY_SKEW_CAL entirely.

The values are taken from the SM8750 vendor camera driver
(csiphy_2ph_v2_4_0_reg); the resulting table matches it entry for entry.
The v2.3.0 table used by the SM8750 CAMSS series carries the same values.

Add the table, a matching SoC config and the qcom,sm8750-csi2-phy match
entry, so SM8750 no longer runs the 4nm lane values. The SoC config keeps
the 3nm common status offset (0x138), like kaanapali.

Signed-off-by: Qianhui Xu <xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
